.TH IEC-CALC 1 "November 2026" "iec-calc 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iec-calc \- analyze IEC consumption exports and rank Israeli electricity plans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iec-calc
.RI [ --debug ]
.RI [ --tariffs " JSON" ]
.BR analyze " | " plans " | " report
.I EXPORT.csv
.RI [ --weather ]
.RI [ --lat " DEG" ]
.RI [ --lon " DEG" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iec-calc
parses an Israel Electric Corp hourly or 15-minute consumption export (CSV)
and computes, interval by interval, the annual cost of every electricity plan
in Israel: the regulated flat tariff, regulated time-of-use (Taoz), and all
private supplier discount plans. Plans are printed cheapest first; the most
worthwhile plan is marked.
.PP
All processing is local. Customer metadata (name, address, contract and
meter numbers) is never printed or logged.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B analyze
Consumption profile: totals, base load, peaks, night/weekend split, anomalies.
.TP
.B plans
Rank all plans by annual cost on your data.
.TP
.B report
Both of the above.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --debug
Verbose diagnostic logging to stderr. Off by default.
.TP
.BI --tariffs " JSON"
Use an alternative tariff catalog instead of the bundled data/tariffs.json.
.TP
.B --phase {single,three}
Meter phase for the fixed-fee calculation (default: single).
.TP
.B --no-smart-meter
Exclude plans that require a smart meter.
.TP
.B --gas
Opt in to gas-customer-only plans (Amisragas); excluded by default.
.TP
.B --hot
Opt in to HOT/NEXT-customer-only plans; excluded by default.
.TP
.BI "--current-plan " LABEL
Mark the plan whose label contains LABEL as your current plan and state the
top plan's annual saving versus it. Must match exactly one plan, including
the regulated options (flat tariff, Taoz); validated before the CSV is read.
.TP
.B --weather
Correlate daily consumption with temperature (Open-Meteo archive API).
Opt-in (off by default). Makes a network call to Open-Meteo. The output is an
experimental estimate only and is never used in the plan ranking.
.TP
.BI --lat " DEG" , --lon " DEG"
Coordinates for weather lookup. Default: 31.78, 35.21 (Jerusalem).
.TP
.BI "--cooling-base " DEG
Cooling degree-day base temperature for the heating/cooling split (default: 22).
.TP
.BI "--heating-base " DEG
Heating degree-day base temperature for the heating/cooling split (default: 18).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on unreadable or empty input.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/tariffs.json
Rates, discount windows, eligibility, source URLs and verification dates.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B iec-calc report export.csv --weather --lat 32.08 --lon 34.78
Full report for Tel Aviv coordinates.
